Zod schemas, like before

170
00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:53.673
for communicating the types of arguments this component is expecting.

171
00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:55.775
You see here, we have a very

172
00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:57.477
long list of components that we're defining.

173
00:07:57.677 --> 00:08:00.446
Title, text, icon, image, and so on and so on.

174
00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:02.548
This is one of the inherent costs of

175
00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:04.517
declarative generative UI. You have to set up

176
00:08:04.517 --> 00:08:08.020
all of your Lego-like building blocks up front

177
00:08:08.321 --> 00:08:10.323
for your agent to be able to assemble them together.

178
00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.325
We won't go through each one of the

179
00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:14.026
components here because essentially they're all the same.

180
00:08:14.227 --> 00:08:15.962
We're now going to define the renderers

181
00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.930
of our components. Once again, we're going to

182
00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:19.799
paste a long file first and

183
00:08:19.799 --> 00:08:21.567
then scroll up and walk through it.

184
00:08:22.068 --> 00:08:24.470
The beginning of the file consists of imports

185
00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.472
that are going to be used by our renderers

186
00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:29.075
and some helper functions once again used by our renderers.

187
00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:32.778
If we scroll a little bit down, we'll see the actual CatalogRenderers.

188
00:08:33.079 --> 00:08:36.282
First you see that the CatalogRenderers is a generic type

