252
00:11:20.546 --> 00:11:23.749
declarative generative UI, where we, as programmers,

253
00:11:23.916 --> 00:11:26.819
hard code a predetermined schema in advance,

254
00:11:26.819 --> 00:11:29.622
which the agent will simply populate with data.

255
00:11:30.356 --> 00:11:32.024
The first step in Fixed Schema Declarative

256
00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:33.959
Generative UI is of course defining the schema.

257
00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.561
Where is the schema going to come from?

258
00:11:35.561 --> 00:11:37.263
Well, you're not going to want to handwrite it.

259
00:11:37.563 --> 00:11:40.933
The schema file is a big messy JSON schema that

260
00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:43.302
is designed to be written by machines.

261
00:11:43.803 --> 00:11:47.506
There's a great tool in the A2UI ecosystem called the A2UI Composer,

262
00:11:47.506 --> 00:11:50.910
which essentially includes a copilot that helps you assemble a schema

263
00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.045
to match some parameters. We're going

264
00:11:53.045 --> 00:11:55.514
to drop screenshots for this A2UI Composer

265
00:11:55.514 --> 00:11:58.317
into the Jupyter notebook, and you can find it on a2ui.org

266
00:11:58.317 --> 00:12:00.019
and then click on the composer.

267
00:12:00.086 --> 00:12:01.287
This picture is what you'll see

268
00:12:01.287 --> 00:12:02.655
when you go to the A2UI Composer.

269
00:12:03.055 --> 00:12:05.958
There's a simple chat input box that lets you specify

270
00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:08.327
the type of component you want to build.

271
00:12:08.327 --> 00:12:10.529
After some iterations, you'll end up with a schema.

272
00:12:10.529 --> 00:12:12.932
The composer shows side by side the schema,

273
00:12:12.932 --> 00:12:16.335
sample data bindings that you can edit if you'd like,

274
00:12:16.335 --> 00:12:18.471
and a preview of what the rendered

275
00:12:18.471 --> 00:12:20.606
schema plus data bindings would look like.

276
00:12:20.606 --> 00:12:23.909
After some iterations, you'll end up with a schema to your liking.

277
00:12:23.909 --> 00:12:25.411
When you've done that, simply copy its

278
00:12:25.411 --> 00:12:26.912
JSON and prepare for the next step.

279
00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:28.914
We're now going to add a tool

280
00:12:28.914 --> 00:12:30.916
that returns a fixed schema

281
00:12:30.916 --> 00:12:32.918
declarative generative UI component.

282
00:12:33.385 --> 00:12:35.454
You will want to paste the

283
00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:37.890
schema definition you got from the composer

284
00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.659
into a variable somewhere in your application.

285
00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.228
If you look here in the

286
00:12:42.228 --> 00:12:43.662
detail, you will see the rough shape

287
00:12:43.863 --> 00:12:45.664
of assembly of components together.

288
00:12:45.865 --> 00:12:46.999
But once again, this is not

289
00:12:46.999 --> 00:12:48.267
code that you want to be handwriting.

290
00:12:48.567 --> 00:12:50.870
Another detail you notice here is the CATALOG_ID

291
00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.671
referencing the component catalog we defined

292
00:12:52.671 --> 00:12:54.673
on the front end, and a SURFACE_ID.

293
00:12:54.774 --> 00:12:57.877
The SURFACE_ID identifies a specific a2ui component.

294
00:12:58.177 --> 00:13:01.580
It's useful because it allows components to be updated, not just

295
00:13:01.914 --> 00:13:05.718
appended to. We're going to create a dummy search_flights tool

296
00:13:06.418 --> 00:13:09.388
for the agent to find relevant flights for this user.

297
00:13:09.688 --> 00:13:11.690
In a real application, this would be

298
00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:13.692
hitting an API or a database, but

299
00:13:13.692 --> 00:13:15.361
for the purposes of example, we're

300
00:13:15.361 --> 00:13:17.296
simply going to hardcode some data here.

301
00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:19.899
Now, we're ready to define the tool that

302
00:13:19.899 --> 00:13:22.601
will return a fixed schema declarative generative UI component.

303
00:13:23.102 --> 00:13:27.873
As you will see, any component whatsoever can return such components.

304
00:13:28.174 --> 00:13:30.176
First, let's look at what this tool returns.

305
00:13:30.376 --> 00:13:33.679
This tool uses the a2ui.render helper function

306
00:13:33.679 --> 00:13:36.182
to return an array of a2ui operations.

307
00:13:36.582 --> 00:13:40.286
The first operation creates a new surface using our SURFACE_ID.

308
00:13:40.386 --> 00:13:44.256
The second operation updates components for that surface using our FLIGHT_SCHEMA.

309
00:13:44.323 --> 00:13:48.427
And finally, the third operation populates the data for the components

310
00:13:48.427 --> 00:13:52.631
using the flights arguments passed to this tool.

311
00:13:52.631 --> 00:13:56.135
Remember, in fixed schema declarative generative UI,

312
00:13:56.135 --> 00:13:58.437
we as programmers predefine the schema.

313
00:13:58.437 --> 00:14:00.840
But it's still the responsibility of the agent

314
00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.942
to populate the data for that schema.

315
00:14:03.008 --> 00:14:04.276
It's critical that the shape of

316
00:14:04.276 --> 00:14:05.811
the data we pass to the component

317
00:14:05.811 --> 00:14:07.813
matches the shape of the data expected by the schema.

318
00:14:08.013 --> 00:14:09.949
In order to ensure this happens, we have

319
00:14:09.949 --> 00:14:11.884
our tool take an array of flight arguments

320
00:14:12.184 --> 00:14:15.788
whose shape exactly matches the shape defined in our schema.

321
00:14:16.288 --> 00:14:19.058
Now that we've defined our tools, it's time to create our agent.

322
00:14:19.458 --> 00:14:22.061
Once again, we're going to create a simple LangChain Deep Agent.

323
00:14:22.361 --> 00:14:23.929
If you look at our list of tools,

324
00:14:23.929 --> 00:14:25.464
you will see the tool we defined previously,

325
00:14:25.564 --> 00:14:27.466
get_sales_data with mock sales data.

326
00:14:27.766 --> 00:14:29.869
as well as two additional tools.

327
00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:32.171
The first one is the search_flights tool,

328
00:14:32.171 --> 00:14:34.473
which provides mock data for flight information.

329
00:14:34.473 --> 00:14:36.375
Once again, in a real application, this would

330
00:14:36.375 --> 00:14:38.544
be connecting to an API or to a database.

331
00:14:38.544 --> 00:14:40.546
as well as the display_flights tool.

332
00:14:40.846 --> 00:14:43.349
The agent can call the display_flights tool

333
00:14:43.349 --> 00:14:47.052
in order to show the A2UI component to the user.

334
00:14:47.052 --> 00:14:49.755
Once again, we specify the CopilotKitMiddleware

335
00:14:49.755 --> 00:14:51.657
and we include a system_prompt that tells

336
00:14:51.657 --> 00:14:53.859
the agent how and when to display components.

337
00:14:53.859 --> 00:14:56.295
If you're curious, you can read this in more detail.

338
00:14:56.295 --> 00:14:58.597
Here, we're adding chat suggestions to

339
00:14:58.597 --> 00:15:01.467
let users easily search for flights.

340
00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.703
Now that we've defined our fixed schema tool,

341
00:15:04.904 --> 00:15:06.906
let's take a look at our application.

342
00:15:07.106 --> 00:15:09.808
The front end is exactly identical to what we saw before.

343
00:15:10.142 --> 00:15:12.044
But now that we've given our agent

344
00:15:12.044 --> 00:15:13.946
the ability to search and display flights,

345
00:15:13.946 --> 00:15:16.949
let's see what happens when we ask it for some flights information.

346
00:15:17.449 --> 00:15:19.118
Good job. The schema you created in

347
00:15:19.118 --> 00:15:21.053
the composer is now live on your screen,

348
00:15:21.353 --> 00:15:24.757
having been populated by the agent. We're now done with this section.

349
00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:28.294
Great job. You now have experience working with declarative generative UI.

350
00:15:28.294 --> 00:15:30.296
You first defined a component catalog,

351
00:15:30.296 --> 00:15:34.566
which is specified by a combination of component definitions and component renderers.

352
00:15:34.566 --> 00:15:37.970
And then exercise that component with both dynamic schema

353
00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:41.473
and fixed schema declarative generative UI. As a reminder,

354
00:15:41.473 --> 00:15:45.311
each declarative generative UI component is specified

355
00:15:45.311 --> 00:15:49.315
by a combination of a schema relative to the component catalog

356
00:15:49.315 --> 00:15:51.684
and data bindings relative to that schema.
